DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_32BC_E69F';
<p>32bc_e69f</p> <p><strong>Deuteranomaly red-green color blindness </strong> is an X-linked recessive genetic disorder that is caused by mutations in the OPN1MW gene. This results in shift in the green retinal receptors toward red wavelength sensitivity. The disorder affects 1 in 20 males and 1 in 400 females of Northern European ancestry. Individuals affected with color blindness have decreased ability to see colors in which they are unable distinguish between shades of red and green. The defective gene for color blindness is located on the long arm of chromosome X at position 28. </p><p><strong>Marfan syndrome (MFS) </strong> is an autosomal dominant genetic disorder that is caused by a mutation in FBN1 gene that makes fibrillin protein. This results in weaked connective tissue throughout the body. The disorder affects 1 in 10,000 people. Individuals affected with MFS have tall and thin features with serious complications involving the heart and aorta. The defective gene for MFS is located on the long arm of chromosome 15 at position 21.1. </p><p>A man (&male;) and a woman (&female;) are planning a family. The man (&male;) does not have color blindness. The woman (&female;) is a carrier for color blindness; her father has color blindness, but her mother does not. The man (&male;) has MFS. The mother (&female;) of the man (&male;) does not have MFS. The woman (&female;) has MFS. The father (&male;) of the woman (&female;) does not have MFS.</p><p>Reminder: color blindness is X-linked recessive and MFS is autosomal dominant.</p><p>What fraction of their daughters (&female;) will have color blindness but not MFS?</p>
PROMPT_32BC_E69F
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_1';
None, 0%
LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_2';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_3';
1/2, 50%
LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_4';
3/4, 75%
LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_5';
All, 100%
LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CORRECT_1';
None, 0%
LITERAL_32BC_E69F_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->buttons\}
END_TEXT
